from pathlib import Path
import hashlib,json
p=Path('.tmp/artifact-integrated-review')
(p/'review.md').write_text('''# Independent artifact-input integration review

HEAD 37fd8fa492249ba2e3755c478daa6382176017ab, base e180e68. No blocking finding in the three reviewed adapters' integration. All 9 committed changed tools/site files match the final exact-byte source snapshots from the individual artifact-input, export and creation-gate reviews. All 53 indexed evidence files in those three seals still match their size/SHA-256 entries. No implementation edits were made.

Independently ran the actual -I export CLI on the parent's saved GitHub artifact ZIP and metadata. Exit 0; the output matched the ZIP's original pages.tar byte-for-byte (1177600 bytes, SHA-256 2237a785ae939072fe659720f2e7a865582185dc01bac4dd76589ba417022bdf). The receipt retained publication_verified false. Using that payload identity in an unresolved creation-intent snapshot still caused the gate to reject; a successful packaging/export receipt is not a deployment receipt and does not resolve creation acceptance. This saved-artifact interoperability run derives pins from the same receipt and does not prove eligible provenance.

The additional uncommitted deployment/README.md clarification was also reviewed and accurately states full-history receipt pairing and the remaining reconciliation duties.

The README connects the boundaries correctly: authenticated download and trusted pins precede offline selected/export validation; the diagnostic artifact ID is not a Pages upload ID; output is a new original-tar file; submit independently checks all creation history before another intent/POST. Run attempt, checks, lock, freshness, actual Pages upload identity, reconciliation and current-publication/LKG decisions remain caller responsibilities. The export's partial-write/host-resource limits and the gate's creation-only scope are disclosed.

Prior individual normal/-O and real-Git failure/boundary results are referenced through verified seals rather than rerunning the entire suite. Root's full-suite run and required CI are separate pending evidence; this review does not approve merging before those requirements finish. No new network call, live API action, deployment or acceptance-state promotion was performed.
''',encoding='utf8',newline='\n')
for row in json.loads((p/'source-match.json').read_text()):
 f=p/'source'/row['path'];f.parent.mkdir(parents=True,exist_ok=True);f.write_bytes(Path(row['path']).read_bytes())
name='tools/site/deployment/README.md'
f=p/'source'/name;f.parent.mkdir(parents=True,exist_ok=True);f.write_bytes(Path(name).read_bytes())
rows=[]
for f in sorted(p.rglob('*')):
 if f.is_file() and f.name!='manifest.json':
  b=f.read_bytes();rows.append(dict(path=f.relative_to(p).as_posix(),bytes=len(b),sha256=hashlib.sha256(b).hexdigest()))
(p/'manifest.json').write_text(json.dumps(dict(source_commit='37fd8fa492249ba2e3755c478daa6382176017ab',files=rows),indent=2)+'\n',encoding='utf8');print(len(rows),sum(x['bytes'] for x in rows))
